    rdf:value """seemed to take great pleasure in gazing into Bernhard’s eyes. Blaydes came to tea with me, and read me part of “La Tentation” in the podere. We had music in the evening. Here is a good story Cook told before we went of a little girl who was taken by her mother to a poultry-yard, and who asked, “Mama, can the hens lay eggs when they like, or  must  they?”
Thursday April 22. 1897. Villa Rosa. Fiesole.
the bottom half of p. 110 struck through and left blank; entries for April 22-28 missing"""^^xsd:string ;
